{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved 63.9% accuracy at 10.60 GPU hours, establishing a baseline. With only one data point, the most impactful uncertainty is whether the image encoder is a bottleneck in the multimodal pipeline. Question: config_006 is a single-variable change from config_001—only the image encoder is upgraded from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L—keeping PCA RNA encoder, average-pool aggregation, weighted fusion, and multiprofile setting identical. This cleanly isolates the contribution of a stronger visual feature extractor, which is likely a major performance driver in cellular imaging where spatial/morphological patterns matter. Rationale: Upgrading the image encoder is the highest-leverage single modification available; if ViT-L meaningfully improves accuracy, it anchors a promising direction for the remaining 8 experiments (e.g., pairing it with better RNA encoders or transformer aggregation). If it does not, we confirm ResNet50 suffices and redirect budget toward RNA-encoder or aggregation upgrades. Expected relative cost: moderate increase over config_001 (ViT-L is ~2× the parameter count of ResNet50), estimated at roughly 14–18 GPU hours, which is acceptable given the high information value of this comparison."
}

